  "findings": [
   "Sun: walls, plunge and the camera 05 deck match within 3%. Camera 07 deck: web 4x (0.149 vs 0.037) although the deck is sunlit in both scenes (ray casts; hiding candidate occluders in Cycles changes nothing). The web deck materials carry roughness 0.5 and default specular while the source uses image/noise roughness 0.5-0.86 and Specular IOR Level 0.28, so the view toward the sun shows a sheen.",
   "V9 with a 60 deg cone: plaster walls 0.58-0.65 of Cycles; with a 90 deg full-penumbra cone 0.9-1.1 in every measured region.",
   "Sky softbox as one shadowed spot light: walls 0.12-0.37 of Cycles. Rays from the wall to the disk center are 82% blocked by V5 light filtering canopy and the web-only restored V5 overhead canopy bough, while the whole 10 m disk is 60-86% visible in both the source scene and the web GLB. Without those two objects in its shadow the spot is 1.3-1.8x Cycles (point light vs disk about 1.27x, remaining partial canopy occlusion).",
   "Glass: Cycles glass passes no direct light. With glass casting shadows the sun and V9 no longer reach the sauna floor (web 0.014/0.020 -> 0.000, Cycles 0.002/0.008).",
   "Sauna interior: Cycles floor and bench light is 88-100% from the interior area lights (under-bench washes etc.); the single web point light gives 0.18-0.25 of it, and raising it lights the cedar walls far above Cycles.",
   "Camera 07 slope: self-shadowed in both scenes (sun below the local horizon); Cycles keeps it at L* 26 through bounce light, the web through the hemisphere light only."
  ]
 },
